  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=342 head=092a9b96f56f22fef3c3e52176f232417b0e0360 -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 342 @ 092a9b96f56f\n\nVERDICT: APPROVED (code=APPROVED, prose=n/a)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-08T10:05:45Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-338-extended-direct-coefficient-loss` onto `issue-327-resampled-coefficient-expectation`; merge base `d33596294e566d4ef26358a5c9bb90d63918fcbe`; head `092a9b96f56f22fef3c3e52176f232417b0e0360`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n<!-- no findings -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nNative review binding: d631d4023b8d4f478ec7c73ac82634fb 092a9b96f56f22fef3c3e52176f232417b0e0360 0f3215ab1af896f3a156f26b4d4e04d40500820edb8262127ef5234833d79a80\n\nReviewed the full canonical diff against the cited paper and blueprint passages. The new theorem correctly reduces the extended losses to `(2m + 3)d/q \u2264 5md/q`, using only positivity of `q`, nonnegativity of `d`, and the admissible consequence `m \u2265 1`. Its statement matches the upstream axis and diagonal coefficient penalties.\n\nThe declaration is accurately classified as a Lean-only scalar auxiliary and does not claim the source theorem or introduce a bridge hypothesis. The inherited line-point identities likewise retain their supplied-witness auxiliary classification.\n\nThe proof-integrity scan found no holes, bypasses, or debug tactics. The new theorem\u2019s axiom audit reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. The worktree is clean and `git diff --check` passes. Existing canonical CI was green and was not rerun. Review provenance: `gpt-5.6-sol`, effort `ultra`.\n",
