  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=342 head=934c65133d0df2a4e0bdb6979c58b8663f8a92a4 -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 342 @ 934c65133d0d\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=APPROVED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-09T04:33:51Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-338-extended-direct-coefficient-loss` onto `issue-327-resampled-coefficient-expectation`; merge base `d33596294e566d4ef26358a5c9bb90d63918fcbe`; head `934c65133d0df2a4e0bdb6979c58b8663f8a92a4`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1112` \u2014 `extendedQ_spec` assumes a supplied witness and is not equivalent to source lemma `qld-4-12`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1078` \u2014 `def:combine-map` retains a stale `\\notready`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/PointsDataProcessing.lean:275` \u2014 four new public coarse-graining and placement results lack a blueprint support node.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/ExtendedCoefficientLoss.lean:23` \u2014 the new scalar estimate lacks a blueprint support entry.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ExtendedLineGame/LinePointRejection.lean:615` \u2014 the two new branch-rejection identities lack blueprint support entries.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/WitnessErrorNonneg.lean:33` \u2014 the three new nonnegativity results lack blueprint support entries.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/CoefficientCollision.lean:45` \u2014 \u201cLean-only auxiliary\u201d uses implementation-oriented terminology.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F8 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree/ExtendedCoefficientLoss.lean:21` \u2014 \u201cLean-only scalar auxiliary\u201d uses implementation-oriented terminology.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F9 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/WitnessErrorNonneg.lean:30` \u2014 the docstrings expose Lean identifiers instead of describing the mathematical objects.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F10 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ExtendedLineGame/LinePointRejection.lean:8` \u2014 the module prose refers directly to `ExtendedLinesWitness`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F11 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ExtendedLineGame/LinePointRejection.lean:363` \u2014 reader-facing prose uses the implementation outcome `none`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nThe changed Lean declarations preserve their intended mathematical scope. In particular, `extendedDirectLd_coefficientCollisionLoss_le_five_mul` is correctly documented as a Lean-only scalar auxiliary, assumes only `AdmissibleParams`, and proves the stated bound using \\(2m+3 \\le 5m\\) for \\(m \\ge 1\\).\n\nStatement-integrity checks found no source drift in `combinePoly_mem_polyFunc`, `combineLinePolynomial_natDegree_le`, `combineLinePoly_spec`, or `extendedQ_spec`. Their additional parameters encode the concrete construction or geometric compatibility data, rather than unproved bridge assumptions. The rejection-transport and witness-error nonnegativity results are also clearly presented as auxiliary lemmas rather than complete paper theorems.\n\nNo new `sorry`, `axiom`, proof bypass, or placeholder tactic was introduced. The three existing `sorry` sites in touched files are known obligations tracked by issues #373 and #388.\n\nVerification completed:\n\n- All changed Lean files type-check individually.\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/DirectLowDegree.lean` passes.\n- `git diff --check`, shell syntax checks, and Python AST compilation pass.\n- The Python unit suite could not create temporary directories under the read-only sandbox; exact-head local CI is reported green.\n\n## Prose review\n\n**F1:** The blueprint states the source existence result, whereas [Points.lean:72](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-338-extended-direct-coefficient-loss/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Points.lean:72) adds `points : CombinedPointsWitness S \u03b4`. This bundled witness is a load-bearing extra assumption, not a boundary condition. Move the links for `extendedQ` and `extendedQ_spec` to a separate formalization-support entry that explicitly states this condition. Keep the source node `\\notready` until a source-faithful existence theorem is available.\n\n**F2:** The declarations linked under `def:combine-map`, including the degree and compatibility specifications, now match the blueprint. The hypothesis `1 \u2264 d` is a faithful boundary condition. Replace `\\notready` with statement-level `\\leanok`.\n\n**F3-F6:** Add subordinate formalization-only blueprint entries for the public declarations at PointsDataProcessing lines 275, 354, 371, and 378; ExtendedCoefficientLoss line 23; LinePointRejection lines 615 and 938; and WitnessErrorNonneg lines 33, 56, and 109. The dependency list at `ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1153` should then reference the affine coarse-graining and placement support actually used, rather than only `fact:data-processing`.\n\n**F7-F8:** Replace \u201cLean-only auxiliary\u201d with \u201cformalization-only auxiliary,\u201d and \u201cLean-only scalar auxiliary\u201d with \u201cformalization-only scalar estimate.\u201d\n\n**F9:** Replace \u201ca supplied `CombinedPointsWitness`\u201d with \u201csupplied combined point measurements\u201d; \u201ca supplied `ExtendedLinesWitness`\u201d with \u201csupplied extended-line measurements\u201d; and \u201con `pairState setting`\u201d with \u201cin the associated paired state.\u201d\n\n**F10:** Replace \u201cstrategy constructed from an `ExtendedLinesWitness`\u201d with \u201cstrategy constructed from the supplied extended-line measurements.\u201d\n\n**F11:** Replace \u201creturning `none`\u201d and \u201cremains the `none` outcome\u201d with \u201creturning the distinguished undefined outcome\u201d and \u201cremains the distinguished undefined outcome \\(\\bot\\).\u201d\n\nThe four `\\Exp` to `\\E` corrections in `ch12_qpbt_games.tex` are consistent with the established expectation notation. Overall: 1 equivalence mismatch, 1 stale status tag, 4 missing-support-entry groups, and 5 prose issues. The equivalence mismatch is the primary blocker.\n",
